        {
          "id": "08e68ca3-fe09-4a32-9973-cbbc6f9d238b",
          "name": "Atlassian Create A Webhook For A Workspace",
          "request": {
            "name": "Atlassian Create A Webhook For A Workspace",
            "description": {
              "content": "Creates a new webhook on the specified workspace.<br><br>Workspace webhooks are fired for events from all repositories contained<br>by that workspace.<br><br>Example:<br><br>```<br>$ curl -X POST -u credentials -H 'Content-Type: application/json'<br>  https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/workspaces/my-workspace/hooks<br>  -d '<br>    {<br>      \"description\": \"Webhook Description\",<br>      \"url\": \"https://example.com/\",<br>      \"active\": true,<br>      \"secret\": \"this is a really bad secret\",<br>      \"events\": [<br>        \"repo:push\",<br>        \"issue:created\",<br>        \"issue:updated\"<br>      ]<br>    }'<br>```<br><br>When the `secret` is provided it will be used as the key to generate a HMAC<br>digest value sent in the `X-Hub-Signature` header at delivery time. Passing<br>a `null` or empty `secret` or not passing a `secret` will leave the webhook's<br>secret unset. Bitbucket only generates the `X-Hub-Signature` when the webhook's<br>secret is set.<br><br>This call requires the webhook scope, as well as any scope<br>that applies to the events that the webhook subscribes to. In the<br>example above that means: `webhook`, `repository` and `issue`.<br><br>The `url` must properly resolve and cannot be an internal, non-routed address.<br><br>Only workspace owners can install webhooks on workspaces.",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "workspaces",
                ":workspace",
                "hooks"
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "type": "any",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "key": "workspace",
                  "description": "(Required) This can either be the workspace ID (slug) or the workspace UUID\nsurrounded by curly-braces, for example: `{workspace UUID}`.\n"
                }
              ]
            },
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": {
              "type": "oauth2",
              "oauth2": [
                {
                  "key": "scope",
                  "value": "read:org:admin write:org:admin read:user:admin write:user:admin read:policy:admin write:policy:admin read:event:admin"
                },
                {
                  "key": "accessTokenUrl",
                  "value": "https://auth.atlassian.com/oauth/token"
                },
                {
                  "key": "authUrl",
                  "value": "https://auth.atlassian.com/authorize"
                },
                {
                  "key": "grant_type",
                  "value": "authorization_code"
                }
              ]
            }
